<title>FRANCE: DETAILS OF FRENCH FREE-MARKET GRAIN BIDS.</title>
<headline>DETAILS OF FRENCH FREE-MARKET GRAIN BIDS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Grain traders bid through France in the following ranges for refunds (Ref.) or taxes to export European Union grain, cereals office ONIC said. ONIC gives the combined tonnage for both tax and refund bids for soft wheat.</p>
<p>			 Aug 14			Jul 31</p>
<p>		Tonnage  Ecu/Tonne	 Tonnage    Ecus/Tonne</p>
<p> Soft wheat 378,500  0.10-1.50  Tax  1,132,500  0.14-2.00  Tax</p>
<p>			   0.00-1.97  Ref.		0.00-14.99 Ref.</p>
<p> Barley     401,000  9.50-19.47 Ref.   398,000  9.90-27.87 Ref.</p>
<p> Rye	  No bids			 No bids</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +331 4221 5146</p>
</text>
